  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) involves comparing the distribution of probabilities: whether more probability mass is assigned to the favorable (positive) outcome relative to zero. In this case, lottery B has a higher probability (0.2% vs 0.1%) of a positive outcome, and although the payoff is smaller (3000 vs 6000), the higher probability suggests a more left-skewed distribution (more weight on the positive side). Thus, B is more left-skewed. The decision reason would prefer B. However, the individual's report does not mention skewness, probability distribution, or any comparison of how the probabilities are spread. Instead, the individual focuses solely on the magnitude of the payoff in case of winning — that A offers double the amount. The individual does not consider the probability of winning or the shape of the distribution. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The justification is based on payoff magnitude, not on skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
